-- title:
--   An ordered deletion cover gives a simplex cover
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be finite with decidable equality and let $H$ be a simplex hypergraph on $n+1$ copies of $G$. If an ordered deletion family covers all occurrences of the associated ordered pattern, its conversion to a simplex deletion family covers every labelled simplex of $H$.
